# Arithmetic with nothing but functions
# In the lambda calculus a number is a function that applies f n times. Everything else is built from that.
# The successor, addition and multiplication of Church numerals:
m:lambda succ = λn f x. f (n f x)
m:lambda plus = λm n f x. m f (n f x)
m:lambda mult = λm n f. m (n f)
# Two is a function that applies f twice. Add one:
m:lambda succ 2
# 2 + 3 is the numeral 5 (apply f five times):
m:lambda plus 2 3
# 3 * 4 is the numeral 12:
m:lambda mult 3 4
# Booleans are functions that choose:
m:lambda true = λa b. a
m:lambda false = λa b. b
m:lambda and = λp q. p q p
m:lambda and true false
# F3 on a line shows every beta step of the reduction:
m:lambda mult 2 2
